this is Lucille Stadium it's the biggest  of qatar's eight World Cup venues  [Music]  and it's on this pitch right here where  one team will win the biggest prize in  football when the final is played here  on December 18th  here's what else you need to know  Lucille Stadium will host 10 matches in  total it seats up to 80 000 fans and  from every single seat in the house  there's an unobstructed view of the pit  it took four years to construct at a  cost of 767 million dollars and it'll be  cooled using solar-powered air  conditioning the roof was made with a  special material that allows just enough  light for the grass on the pitch to grow  while still providing enough shade to  keep temperatures down the use of Lights  and Shadows was inspired by the  traditional Arabic Lantern while the  shape and intricate gold exterior was  influenced by decorative bowls and art  across the region the stadium is in the  newly developed blue Sail City right  outside of Doha it can be reached by the  Metro's Red Line in the city's Light  Rail tram  after the World Cup the stadium will be  downsized around 20 000 seats from the  upper tier will be removed and the area  will be transformed into a community  center with housing shops and  restaurants but before that happens  there's plenty of football to be played  and football history to be made
 

